# 6. Use the GPU correctly and present each output independently

[Organization and execution order](record:r_0PCR2DTXNGTQGBE6RBWR0ECTXW). Targets are in [benchmarks](record:r_7CWV5KN1695FW2KNPGW5X19PJ7); interaction coverage is in [workflows](record:r_33DFSQHTZFRCM758HHPN3KRWNA).

Current instruction: source-only removal of known unnecessary work; no compilation, GPU checks, runtime measurements, shipping or restart. For a later authorized execution phase, follow [12](record:r_7NBQGTF152S58NPT0Z9EM58C1T): reuse completed frame/device instrumentation, finish P153/P70/P67 consumer evidence, and evaluate source-identified production changes without old/new path switches. Private Niri results do not close physical Park gates. The former blanket compilation permission is superseded.

This stage is coupled to input, retained presentation and output clocks. P67/P70 must distinguish actual software pixel work, CPU submission, hardware execution, synchronization and repeated copies. A low-utilization GPU does not establish wrong processor placement. Client-only native-frame reuse already exists. Reuse valid prior surfaces/resources and present the latest coherent frame without accumulating latency.

Start with the largest traced cost. Direct scanout is conditional late work for eligible fullscreen clients; it cannot solve native editing/saving. Do not make every window eligible by disabling overlays, transformations, capture or color precision. Bevy rendering is already GPU-backed; an entirely new renderer is justified only by evidence that the existing integration cannot meet the shared budgets. Preserve actual GPU/native thread affinity and every submitted consumer lifetime.

**Implemented, verification pending (2026-11-17):** secondary-output/overview synchronization now borrows current source data, reuses query and vertex preparation, and skips identical render-component publication. OUTPUT-PREPARATION-VERIFY/OUTPUT-PUBLICATION-VERIFY/OUTPUT-VERTEX-VERIFY in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) cover both outputs, previews, holes, clipping and resource retirement. Mesh creation was already conditional on geometry changes; a borrowed material comparison removes mutable resource access and handle copying, not an established material upload. These CPU-side changes do not establish GPU execution, damage-retention, DMA-BUF or frame-overlap gains.

**Implemented, verification pending (2026-11-17):** transparent same-plane ordering and decoration attachment reuse cleared render-system scratch. Current extracted order/anchor maps are built together; disorder is detected once while grouping. Decorations skip sorting when no relevant anchor exists or exact ranks are already ordered. Stable comparison, original group slots and the underlying engine depth order are retained. STACKING-PREPARATION-VERIFY in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) owns pixel/order, retirement and complete-cost checks. This is separate from Bevy UI stacking and does not establish GPU or layout savings.

**Implemented, verification pending (2026-11-17):** terrain fields, tiles and overview ground share immutable Input/Formula ownership, compare current values before replacement allocation and reuse unchanged physical fields. Preview rendering copies only affected workspace vectors and restores the original physical state. Full-definition preview compilation, including refusals, is retained only while selected and eligible; current placement, faults and owner checks remain. TERRAIN-INPUT-OWNERSHIP-VERIFY/TERRAIN-PREVIEW-RESTORE-VERIFY/TERRAIN-PREVIEW-COMPILE-VERIFY in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) cover these CPU-side changes. They do not establish GPU completion, fewer required mesh uploads or end-to-end gains.

**Implemented, verification pending (2026-11-17):** terrain collider and visual mesh consumers share ordered vertex/triangle iterators. Required final buffers remain owned, while intermediate world-position/triangle vectors and clipped-only discarded UV/index preparation are removed. Stack quads avoid duplicate clipping-comparison allocations; clipping arithmetic and output density remain. Primary/overview material preparation is shared within the call, and unchanged overview/hidden-ground component writes are skipped. Three TERRAIN- preparation/publication checks in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) own verification. These CPU-side reductions do not establish GPU savings or change the output synchronization model.

**Implemented, verification pending (2026-11-17):** appearance lighting selects only current Surface+Light participants, avoids disabled/no-candidate preparation and stops after the existing admitted-light budget. Sorted priority, live-hole visibility, light math, shadows and restoration remain. Idle texture Jobs are not detached/reinserted; active settlement transfers keys while preserving import/worker ownership and wakeups. Rounded plate meshes read existing U16/U32/unindexed triangles without an intermediate index vector; geometry arithmetic and required final buffers remain. Unchanged mesh/shadow-map writes are skipped. APPEARANCE-LIGHTING-VERIFY/APPEARANCE-TEXTURE-VERIFY/APPEARANCE-GEOMETRY-VERIFY in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) cover these CPU-side changes; no GPU-placement, damage-retention or visual-quality gain is claimed.

**Implemented, verification pending (2026-11-17):** room compositing derives exact root/workspace/room ordinals from borrowed current sources once per extraction. Render snapshots own ordinals rather than per-entity room-string copies. Clouds are prepared only for rooms with current floor-overlay/foreground consumers, preserving last-wins duplicate scene mappings; previous base-bias restoration retains its original one-frame role and precedence. Each output uses reusable nearest-distance slots, clearing only touched rooms, and skips cloud/reapplication scans when no relevant cloud exists. ROOM-COMPOSITING-VERIFY in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) covers exact depth math/order, readable text, multi-output isolation, source changes and total interner/scratch cost. This is CPU preparation, not a GPU placement or scanout change.

**Implemented, verification pending (2026-11-17):** main-world stacking input preparation shares sibling ordinals and focused application ancestry within a fresh immutable pass. Primary surfaces and secondary output instances publish prepared keys; pointer geometry uses the same derivation. Prefix indexes stop at current demand, preserve first-child/application precedence and never survive source mutation. Candidate transient validation and the 32-step limit remain. STACKING-INPUTS-VERIFY in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) covers output/hit-order parity, freshness and complete allocation/CPU cost. This removes repeated CPU derivation, not rendering, GPU submission or required paint.

**Continue through these Records:**

- [P53 — Verify implemented output demand and callback pacing.](record:r_3HT09KTMPBS113E9QXKT5ASZGQ)
- [P55 — Remove one measured redundant render pass or copy.](record:r_7P9VMMCDVV7ZN72MVSTZ3CHF4J)
- [P68 — Compare processor placement for one evidenced misplaced stage.](record:r_7NEHBEAZ041VSG76B4TAWJ83PS)
- [P52 — Retain damage independently for each output.](record:r_0R0MWH247WFE7SYBX74GP66PM8)
- [P81 — Retain compatible incoming DMA-BUF import bindings.](record:r_3NRE33E28Y9X36N8D8VJ6WC1Z1)
- [P54 — Reuse compatible exported/output resources within a bounded budget.](record:r_6DMZQYSZSS9119FGZY71NC5TYE)
- [P59 — Reduce measured raster-resolution churn during navigation.](record:r_6YRB2V4SHY7M6SN3NDXWKJ8YYZ)
- [P57 — Test direct scanout for one eligible fullscreen SDR client.](record:r_1W82JGD8E7MYX2XM60YYXGMM53)
} r_333RCJBDSGX0Y0W630FWHJAJCB

P53 — Verify implemented output demand and callback pacing. (
    @park-p53: 0,
    is #task,
    #park-performance-task,
    #park-stage-a1,
    #part-of @park-dev-06-gpu-and-outputs: 12,
    #park-workflow @park-development-cycle
) { r_3HT09KTMPBS113E9QXKT5ASZGQ
**Status — implemented, physical verification pending.** Successful-output callback ownership and the bounded per-output estimated-refresh/no-damage queue are already coded. They preserve replacement deadlines, pause/mode changes and stale-owner retirement. Do not build them again.

**Still to verify:** independent output activity, quiet/off-screen clients, actual callback traffic, missed deadlines, failure/resume, multi-node GPU coherence and ready work while an earlier submission is stalled. Compare frame age and physical output intervals. Zero no-damage counter activity is not a speedup. Preserve input, semantic work and capture service independently of another output.

**Why:** callback service must follow actual output demand without an immediate redraw loop or a global polling clock. The physical daily desktop remains unverified even where private compositor checks passed. Execution is deferred by the current source-only instruction; use Overhaul.md and the current checkpoint.

} r_3HT09KTMPBS113E9QXKT5ASZGQ

